1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,150
A menu is a list of menu items, and the Menu module provides

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:06,785
three types of them.

3
00:00:06,785 --> 00:00:10,746
In this video, we add a link, a content item, and an HTML

4
00:00:10,746 --> 00:00:13,890
item to a menu, and choose who sees an item.

5
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:21,922
A Link Menu Item links to an address you type.

6
00:00:21,922 --> 00:00:25,816
A Content Menu Item links to a content item you pick.

7
00:00:25,816 --> 00:00:30,172
An Html Menu Item links to an address, and shows HTML as the

8
00:00:30,172 --> 00:00:31,690
text of the link.

9
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:35,243
Link and Html items have a Permissions field.

10
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:39,420
People who do not have the permissions you choose do not see the item.

11
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:44,214
A Content Menu Item has the option Check content permissions instead.

12
00:00:44,214 --> 00:00:48,690
It hides the item from people who may not view the content item it points to.

13
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:53,693
The HTML of an Html Menu Item is cleaned when the menu is

14
00:00:53,693 --> 00:00:56,596
displayed, to prevent custom scripts.

15
00:00:56,596 --> 00:01:01,390
The Sanitize Html setting controls this, and it is on by default.

16
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:08,755
Under Content, Menus, open the Main Menu.

17
00:01:08,755 --> 00:01:13,386
A separate video covers creating menus and arranging their items.

18
00:01:13,386 --> 00:01:17,430
Here, the Add Menu Item button adds an item to this one.

19
00:01:17,888 --> 00:01:21,694
The Available Menu Items window lists the three types:

20
00:01:21,694 --> 00:01:25,437
Link Menu Item, Content Menu Item and Html Menu Item.

21
00:01:25,437 --> 00:01:27,848
Each one has its own Add button.

22
00:01:32,148 --> 00:01:33,941
Let's add a Link Menu Item.

23
00:01:33,941 --> 00:01:37,038
It has a Name, which is the text of the link, and a

24
00:01:37,038 --> 00:01:38,940
Url that says where it leads.

25
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:42,418
We name it Editor Guide, and link it to the documentation.

26
00:01:46,158 --> 00:01:48,431
Target says where the link opens.

27
00:01:48,431 --> 00:01:52,975
It suggests values, and one of them opens the linked document in another

28
00:01:52,975 --> 00:01:55,538
window or tab, so the site stays open.

29
00:01:56,027 --> 00:01:58,451
Publish adds the item to the menu.

30
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:02,147
The menu editor lists it with its name and its address.

31
00:02:06,447 --> 00:02:08,915
Add Menu Item opens the same window.

32
00:02:08,915 --> 00:02:14,027
This time we choose Content Menu Item, which links to a content item of the site.

33
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,572
Name is the text of the link, so we type Hours.

34
00:02:17,572 --> 00:02:22,590
In Selected Content Item, we type to search, and pick the Opening Hours article.

35
00:02:23,069 --> 00:02:24,819
No address is typed here.

36
00:02:24,819 --> 00:02:28,659
The link is built from the content item itself, so it leads to

37
00:02:28,659 --> 00:02:30,409
the address of that item.

38
00:02:30,875 --> 00:02:34,640
Check content permissions stays off for a public page.

39
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:39,723
Turn it on for restricted content, and cache the menu, as its hint advises.

40
00:02:39,723 --> 00:02:41,795
Then Publish adds the item.

41
00:02:46,037 --> 00:02:50,636
The third type, the Html Menu Item, has the same Name, Url and

42
00:02:50,636 --> 00:02:54,897
Target fields as a link, and one more field for the HTML.

43
00:03:00,388 --> 00:03:04,027
Let's name it Contact us, and link it to an email address, so

44
00:03:04,027 --> 00:03:07,448
that selecting it opens the email program of the visitor.

45
00:03:07,909 --> 00:03:11,718
The Html field replaces the name as the text of the link, and

46
00:03:11,718 --> 00:03:13,253
sits inside the link.

47
00:03:13,253 --> 00:03:15,469
Let's make the first word italic.

48
00:03:15,957 --> 00:03:22,069
The HTML is cleaned when the menu is displayed, because Sanitize Html is on by default.

49
00:03:22,069 --> 00:03:24,697
Publish adds the item to the menu.

50
00:03:28,971 --> 00:03:31,584
To restrict an item, choose Edit on its row.

51
00:03:31,584 --> 00:03:36,391
Let's restrict Editor Guide, because it is meant for the people who work in the admin.

52
00:03:36,844 --> 00:03:41,035
In Permissions, we type to search, and select Access admin panel.

53
00:03:41,035 --> 00:03:44,341
Only people who have this permission see the item.

54
00:03:44,341 --> 00:03:47,764
When you choose several, a person needs all of them.

55
00:03:48,234 --> 00:03:51,884
A restricted item hides the items under it as well.

56
00:03:51,884 --> 00:03:54,574
Publish adds the change to the menu.

57
00:03:58,807 --> 00:04:02,331
Each change is saved in a draft of the menu, so the site

58
00:04:02,331 --> 00:04:06,537
keeps showing the published menu until the menu itself is published.

59
00:04:08,521 --> 00:04:11,452
Let's publish the Main Menu with the Publish button.

60
00:04:11,452 --> 00:04:16,151
A message confirms that your Menu has been published, and the editor stays on the menu.

61
00:04:16,609 --> 00:04:21,703
On the site, signed in as the administrator, the menu lists Home, About,

62
00:04:21,703 --> 00:04:26,469
Editor Guide, Hours and Contact us, with the first word in italics.

63
00:04:28,090 --> 00:04:32,282
A visitor who is not signed in gets the same menu without Editor Guide.

64
00:04:32,282 --> 00:04:35,820
The other items have no permissions, so everyone sees them.

65
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:42,750
That is how Link, Content and Html menu items work, and how permissions

66
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:44,479
decide who sees them.

67
00:04:44,479 --> 00:04:47,936
A separate video covers how themes render menus.

68
00:04:47,936 --> 00:04:49,600
Thanks for watching.

